				},
				"string" : "## Layered design"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-04-11T22:22:36.39618-04:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-04-11T22:25:33.618694-04:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "evgZJ9ZZSC6WCzm56TT0UA=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Key classes (planned)\n\n- **`Gt4SecurityOsvClient`** — POST `api.osv.dev/v1/query`, GET `/v1/vulns/{id}`. Methods: `queryAndroidBulletin:`, `queryEcosystem:package:`, `vulnerabilityById:`.\n- **`Gt4SecurityNvdClient`** — GET `services.nvd.nist.gov/rest/json/cves/2.0`. Methods: `cvesModifiedSince:`, `cvesForCpe:`, `cveById:`. Config holds optional API key.\n- **`Gt4SecurityVulnerability`** — normalized record (`id`, `summary`, `severity`, `publishedAt`, `modifiedAt`, `ecosystem`, `affectedPackages`, `references`, `rawSource`).\n- **`Gt4SecurityVulnerabilityGroup`** — uses `TGtGroupWithItems` for an inspectable collection with filter views (by ecosystem, severity, date).\n- **`Gt4SecurityQuery`** — builder-style query that can fan out to OSV + NVD and merge results by CVE id.\n- **`Gt4SecurityExamples`** — `<gtExample>` methods hitting live endpoints with tight assertions (skipped when offline).\n\n## GT views\n\nEvery domain object gets `<gtView>` views for exploration. Minimum set per class:\n\n- `gtVulnerabilitiesFor: aView` — columned list (id, severity, published, ecosystem)\n- `gtAffectedFor: aView` — affected packages / CPEs\n- `gtReferencesFor: aView` — linkified references\n- `gtRawFor: aView` — raw JSON for debugging\n\n## Config\n\nFollow the pattern from other gt4* projects:\n\n- Class-side `Gt4Security class >> default` singleton\n- Instance vars for API keys (NVD), user-agent string\n- Never read secrets from `.envrc` — caller supplies keys via `default nvdApiKey: aString`"
			}
		]
	},
